// GHZ.QS0 - a three-qubit Greenberger-Horne-Zeilinger state.
//
// Demonstrates: superposition, entanglement, measurement correlation,
// and the stabilizer engine.
//
// Qubit-level explanation:
//   Start in |000>.
//   H 0      puts qubit 0 into the equal superposition (|0>+|1>)/sqrt2,
//            so the state becomes (|000>+|100>)/sqrt2.
//   CNOT 0 1 entangles qubit 1 with qubit 0: |000> stays, |100> -> |110>,
//            giving (|000>+|110>)/sqrt2.
//   CNOT 1 2 entangles qubit 2 with qubit 1, giving the GHZ state
//            (|000>+|111>)/sqrt2.
//
// Measuring every qubit always yields all-zero or all-one. The histogram is
// a 50/50 split between |000> and |111> with no mixed outcomes, which is a
// direct test of multi-partite entanglement: the three measurement results
// are perfectly correlated even though each individual qubit is maximally
// mixed.
//
// Run (all give the same 50/50 split):
//   plasma run examples/GHZ.QS0 --shots 1000
//   plasma run examples/GHZ.QS0 --gpu --shots 1000
//   plasma run examples/GHZ.QS0 --stabilizer --shots 1000
// The stabilizer engine handles this Clifford circuit exactly.
QUBITS 3
H 0
CNOT 0 1
CNOT 1 2
SHOT 1000
PRINT
END